ting the seat and then  leave and have a  really really safe experience and so  that's still currently where we are  um and my my suspicion  is you know the the vaccine rollout has  been great and  you know as we reach that point where  everybody in the united states has had  access to the vaccine  that to me triggers the point where okay  um  now everybody has the opportunity to be  vaccinated significant percentage of  folks have been  so we'll return to normal you know we're  estimating that's hopefully  in in q3 later this year and we'll be  cautious up until that point  gotcha gotcha there's always been some  speculation among industry watchers that  theaters were  are going to have to start offering more  of a premium experience uh on the other  side of this pandemic to really  entice audiences to come back even with  all the safety precautions that you just  laid out  your chain is known for its food for its  lux seating  and for the strict no phones policy  which i applaud um but that was before  the pandemic  what do you think it'll take now in  terms of offering new experiences to  keep  people coming back in on a consistent  basis  well for us that's really been our core  product right i i came into this  business as a total outsider with no  experience other than really loving  movies and  we've carried that forward now i have  you know some experience  but um you know the idea of premium  it's not always premium what we want to  do is just make sure that  every touch point we have with our  guests from from the website to entering  the door  to sitting down to the food you eat the  drinks to the quality of the  presentation like everything is  beautiful  and worth getting out of the home so  you know there's there's been a lot of  talk about about streamers and the  effect that's going to have on the  industry and  i don't i don't really see it that way i  see  we're in the out of home entertainment  business and so  we need to ensure that if you make a